• Record Delimited by: Character that separates data record rows. As an example, you can choose to use
next line (\n) if the next set of records is in the next row.
 Example
FIELD1;FIELD2;
PROD01;CUST01;
PROD02;CUST02;
Another example is to use the equal sign (=) if sets of records are divided by the = character.
 Example
FIELD1;FIELD2;=CUST;PROD;=PROD01;PROD02;
• Field Delimited by: Character that separates columns. Usually, in a CSV file, fields are separated by a
comma (,) or semi-colon (;).
 Example
FIELD1;FIELD2;
PROD01;CUST01;
PROD02;CUST02;
• Whitelist Path: Directory or path on your application server where the file is available.
 Note
For more information about how to set up the whitelist path, see SAP Note 2910484 .
